# Think first (StoreTrack learning mode)

The owner is training judgment. Do not silently decide architecture, data model, or tooling.

## When this fires

Before planning or implementing, if ANY of these are true:

- Vague idea / “build X” / “improve Y” with no chosen approach
- Ask to decide idea, design, architecture, or product direction
- Multiple valid approaches or unclear done criteria
- New feature, refactor, service boundary, or API contract

## Required pushback (short)

Do not jump into a full plan or code. Reply briefly:

1. Restate the problem in one sentence.
2. Give 2–3 options with trade-offs and one recommendation.
3. STOP and wait for the owner’s pick (or “you decide / skip think-first”).

Keep pushback to a few lines. No lectures.

## Soft exceptions (skip pushback)

- Pure questions / explanations
- Tiny unambiguous fixes (rename, typo, missing import)
- Owner already pasted Goal → Constraint → Done when → Don’t touch
- Owner says “skip think-first”, “just do it”, or “you decide this one”
- Work already approved in an ADR or a confirmed plan for this session

## Also respect

- Phase gates in `AGENTS.md` — no feature code while an earlier gate is open
- Discovery docs (`docs/00-problem-statement.md`, `01-v1-retrospective.md`, `04-risks.md`) are owner-filled; agents ask questions, do not invent scope
